# Line endings (issue #516).
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out with CRLF unless a
# rule here says otherwise. Most files don't care. Files that a Linux shell or Docker reads do:
# a CRLF docker/entrypoint.sh stops the container from starting, and a CRLF
# packages/core/bootstrap/agent.sh breaks setup on every Server. scripts/check-line-endings.mjs
# fails the lint if a shell script is not covered by the eol=lf rules below.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Terminal recordings stored byte-for-byte, CRLF included. Leave them alone.
docs/history/spike/recordings/*.txt -text

# Use bd merge for beads JSONL files
.beads/issues.jsonl merge=beads
